\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O for a heart to praise my God, 
\par A heart from sin set free,
\par A heart that alway feels Thy blood
\par So freely spilt for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A heart resigned, submissive, meek,
\par My great redeemer's throne,
\par Where only Christ is heard to speak,
\par Where Jesus reigns alone:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. A humble, lowly, contrite heart,
\par Believing, true and clean;
\par Which neither life nor death can part
\par From Him that dwells within:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. A heart in every thought renewed,
\par And full of love divine;
\par Perfect, and right, and pure, and good,
\par A copy, Lord, of Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy nature, gracious Lord, impart;
\par Come quickly from above,
\par Write Thy new name upon my heart,
\par Thy new, best name of love.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

